# Step 28, skills: finding them in the project's and the user's folders,
# reading their front matter, and listing them in section 6 of the system
# prompt (`crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs`). Each rule broken on its own,
# with the tests that must fail. Written with the code
# (docs/steps/28/answered.md, point 7).

[break] compat-off-still-reads-other-tools-folders
rule: Without `compat.skills`, `.agents/skills/` and `.claude/skills/` are not looked in.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: Root::standard
find: layout.is_compat() && !compat
replace: false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::the_standard_roots_in_the_order_a_name_is_taken
    cineris-ext skills::tests::skills_are_found_one_level_down_in_every_root_and_listed_by_name

[break] a-projects-root-may-lead-out-of-the-workspace
rule: A project's root is looked in only where it leads to a place inside the workspace: what a repository's link reaches is not the repository's.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: open_root
find: root.owner == Owner::Project && !location_within(&real, &places.workspace)
replace: false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_root_that_is_a_link_is_followed_and_a_projects_only_inside_the_workspace
    cineris-ext skills::tests::roots_written_with_a_tilde_a_relative_path_and_dots_lead_to_the_same_skills

[break] a-users-root-is-held-to-the-workspace
rule: The user's root is followed wherever it leads: the user named it.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: open_root
find: root.owner == Owner::Project && !location_within(&real, &places.workspace)
replace: !location_within(&real, &places.workspace)
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::skills_are_found_one_level_down_in_every_root_and_listed_by_name
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_root_that_is_a_link_is_followed_and_a_projects_only_inside_the_workspace

[break] one-folder-is-looked-at-twice
rule: A root that is the same folder as one looked at before it, however it is written, is not looked at again.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: open_root
find: same_location(earlier, &real)
replace: same_location(earlier, &real) && false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::roots_written_with_a_tilde_a_relative_path_and_dots_lead_to_the_same_skills

[break] a-link-to-nothing-is-not-said
rule: A link to nothing is left out, and said to be one.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: path_reason
find: PathError::DanglingLink { .. } => Reason::Dangling
replace: PathError::DanglingLink { .. } => Reason::Unreadable(String::new())
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_link_to_nothing_and_a_skill_file_that_is_no_file_are_left_out

[break] a-root-is-read-past-its-entry-cap
rule: At most 1,000 entries are looked at in a root, and the rest are said not to have been.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: look_in
find: names.len() == MAX_ENTRIES
replace: false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_root_with_more_than_a_thousand_entries_is_looked_at_only_so_far

[break] a-folder-linked-out-of-its-root-is-followed
rule: A skill's folder reached through a link is followed only where it stays below its root: not out of it, and not to the root itself.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: skill_in
find: if !inside
replace: if false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_link_in_a_root_that_leads_out_of_it_is_left_out

[break] a-skill-file-linked-out-of-its-root-is-read
rule: A `SKILL.md` reached through a link is read only where it stays inside its root.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: skill_in
find: !location_within(&file.to_fs_path(), &root)
replace: false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_link_in_a_root_that_leads_out_of_it_is_left_out

[break] a-skill-file-that-is-no-file-is-passed-over
rule: A `SKILL.md` that is a folder, a FIFO or a device is left out with its reason.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: read_capped
find: Err(OpenError::Directory | OpenError::NotAFile) => return Err(Reason::NotAFile)
replace: Err(OpenError::Directory | OpenError::NotAFile) => return Ok(None)
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_link_to_nothing_and_a_skill_file_that_is_no_file_are_left_out

[break] a-skill-file-past-its-cap-is-read
rule: A `SKILL.md` larger than 64 KiB is left out.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: read_capped
find: bytes.len() as u64 > MAX_SKILL_BYTES
replace: false
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_skill_file_larger_than_64_kib_is_left_out

[break] the-skill-files-cap-is-not-64-kib
rule: The cap on a `SKILL.md` is 64 KiB.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
find: pub const MAX_SKILL_BYTES: u64 = 64 * 1024;
replace: pub const MAX_SKILL_BYTES: u64 = 65 * 1024;
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_skill_file_larger_than_64_kib_is_left_out

[break] a-nameless-skill-is-listed
rule: A `SKILL.md` whose front matter gives no name, or one that is empty once it is one line, is left out.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: skill_in
find: skill_name.is_empty()
replace: false
